WEBVTT

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.920
What is the meaning of this?

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.250
Of what?

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.420
"Of whaaaat?"

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.800
Don't play coy with me!
Why have they already left?

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.300
Their departure date was
moved up, apparently.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.890
Why wasn't I informed?!

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.180
Because I didn't inform you.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.140
Why should I have?
You wouldn't have been able to go, anyway.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.810
I <i>am </i>the Grand Magus of this Assembly.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.190
Is that so?

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.730
Then please, finish his work for me.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:32.950
Ser, the Second Order of Knights has sent
a missive urgently requesting our help...

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:44.460
As new recruits, your work will primarily
involve research here in our offices.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.040
As many of your colleagues
require intense focus for their work,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.250
please work quietly so
as to not disturb them.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.260
Yes, ser!

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.510
Get back here! Right this instant!

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.100
Don't you dare try to escape your duties!

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.740
I know you. You're from
the same world as Sei, yes?

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:18.910
Y-Yes, ser.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.660
Let's be off.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.040
Huh?

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:00.050
Predicament

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.310
Jude.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.350
Director Johan.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.690
The Grand Magus.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.980
Liz.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.230
Aira.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.730
Mary.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.860
The Knights.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.030
Commander Hawke.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:26.990
Stop, stop, stop!

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:29.410
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:37.800
Yes?

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.720
Lady Sei?

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:44.090
Would you care to break for some tea?

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.890
Th-Thank you, that sounds lovely.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.240
I know you do this all the time,
but you're so good at what you do.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.120
Thank you for the kind compliment.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.120
I don't think too much about it,

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:13.790
so suddenly calling attention to it
makes me feel truly flattered.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.670
You don't think too much about it?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:21.880
Yes. Being skilled at my many
duties is simply part of my job.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.220
Just part of your job...

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.270
If I treat it like part of my job, then I
won't have to think too hard about it!

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.660
There you are.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.660
Hello. I'm looking forward to
working with you again today.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.620
Actually, could I ask for your help?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.580
What is it?

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.750
You want to experiment with your blessing?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:02.710
Yes. I was hoping you
might have a few ideas...

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.350
Follow me.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:26.660
First, let's test it on
these potted plants.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.370
All right, I'll give it a try!

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.630
What's wrong?

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.130
N-Nothing, nothing's wrong!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:50.300
This is my job. My job!
Just my job, just my job...

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.940
The blessing!

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.950
Did it work?

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.750
I'm not sure. I was able to cast it,
at the very least.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.790
All right.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:24.710
If it didn't work, then these seeds won't
sprout. We'll keep an eye on them.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.170
All right.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.930
Right, then.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.050
Next, do this one.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.350
When you're done,
move to this one, then this one.

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.020
Huh?

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.490
Good work.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.200
Thank you, ma'am.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:54.950
These'll grow fast, so we'll see
sprouts in two or three days.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:59.080
I'll come by to check on
them tomorrow, just in case.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.290
Yes, that's a good idea.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.710
Hey, there she is!

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:04.750
Yo!

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:11.050
Join my mercenary company!

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.590
What?

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.180
Please!

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.260
Uh...

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:18.600
Remember how you healed
a whole bunch of us?

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.650
Well, we don't see mages that can
use healing magic all that often!

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.810
Alchemy's a waste of your talents,
I'm telling you!

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:28.860
Hold it! What do you mean,
alchemy's a waste?!

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.320
Oh, I don't mean that alchemy's
not helpful or anything!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:37.950
But I'd be stupid if I let a high-level
healing caster go without tryin'!

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:43.210
I know they're few and far between,
and I see where you're coming from.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.210
So you get it!

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:46.460
But you need to give up on Sei!

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:47.550
But <i>why</i>?

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:52.680
She can make potions
<i>and </i>cast healing magic!

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.930
You see people that powerful
once in a lifetime!

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.350
I'm not just gonna let her walk away!

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.640
What do you think you're doing?

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:06.190
Just having a brief chat with her, milord.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:08.730
I see. And what was it
you were discussing?

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.320
Nothing of importance, milord.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:15.700
Poppycock. You were just asking her
to join your mercenary company.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:16.830
Granny!

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.200
Sei will do nothing of the sort.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:24.580
And why's that your choice, huh?
You've got nothing to do with her.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:29.210
On the contrary, I do.
She came here with us from the capital.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:33.840
What? So she's with the
Royal Magi Assembly, then?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.050
Why's a mage like her
making potions for...

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.890
Wait,

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.100
are you the Saint?!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.150
That's the Lady Saint to you, dimwit!

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.940
Did I forget to tell you?

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.690
Everyone did, apparently!

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:54.450
As such, she will not be able
to join your mercenary company.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.410
Was there anything else you
wished to speak with her about?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.370
Uh, no, milord.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.500
Then might I have her attention?

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:05.460
I have something to discuss with her.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.420
I'll take my leave, then.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.760
Thank you for taking the time to help
me today. I really appreciate it.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:15.880
You're always welcome.
I learned plenty, too.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:18.010
I'll see you later.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.720
Come on, you!

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:25.730
Ow! Be gentle!
You're gonna rip off my ear!

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.160
So, what was it you wanted to discuss?

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.370
Right. We've finished our
initial scouting of the area,

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:43.830
so we'd like to begin our
expeditions into the woods.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:47.540
I assume that means I'll be
joining you from here on out.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:53.670
Yes. Though we have mages accompanying
us, not many can cast healing magic.

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:57.260
I regret that we have
to ask for your help.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.010
It's all right. I'd planned
on coming along, anyway.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:02.010
The monsters in the area
are quite powerful,

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:05.480
but we shouldn't encounter
hordes of them all at once.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:09.480
We still have yet to discover one
of those dark swamps, however.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.230
I see...

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:16.280
I thought getting rid of that one
would solve all of our problems.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:20.490
And working myself up to cast the
blessing is really, really annoying...

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.780
What's wrong?

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:22.990
Huh?

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:26.620
You look flushed. Are you feeling well?

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.920
I-I'm quite all right, thank you!

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.420
Really? If you're feeling unwell, we can--

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.840
No, I'm totally fine! Honest!

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.310
How the heck do I explain it to him?

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.100
I can't. Not yet.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.500
Huh? Teatime for you, too, Ser?

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:11.670
Same for you, then?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:19.340
I always start to crave tea
right around this time.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:23.140
At some point, it just became
part of my routine.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.220
Right?

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.390
I wonder what she's up to.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:31.140
The usual, I expect.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:45.280
Boy, I'd heard the rumors,
but you sure are one of a kind, huh?

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.700
What rumors?

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:51.460
Oh, I heard some randos sayin' how the new
girl can craft loads of potions in one go.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.830
Which "randos" are talking about that?

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:58.760
My apologies, I need to
mind my tone, milady.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.010
Huh?

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:02.010
Wait, is that not what you meant?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:03.510
What did you think I meant?

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:09.180
I thought you were offended by the tone
I was taking with you, the Lady Saint.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.810
Not at all. You don't have to
be formal with me.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:16.230
I'd actually prefer it if you didn't.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:19.900
Is that right?
Well, then, I won't change a thing.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.610
Thanks.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:24.740
This is way easier on me, too.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:27.620
I'm terrible at formalities
and manners 'n all that.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.870
Oh, yeah, you going on that expedition?

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:33.920
Yes. That <i>is </i>why I came all this way.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:39.420
I know you've been on expeditions before,
but I can't help but worry 'bout you.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.260
You mean if we encounter monsters?

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.760
The forests out here are way more
dangerous than the ones

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.010
surrounding the capital.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:49.720
There might be fewer monsters as of late,
but there are still loads of 'em.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:55.310
Well, I'm sure I'll be all right.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:57.980
I'm tougher than you might expect.

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:04.030
You're brimmin' with confidence,
aren'tcha? Hope I didn't insult you.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.240
No, it's all right.
Thank you for worrying about me.

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.960
Will we be heading out
once we're all gathered?

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:26.220
Yes. We'll head out after
I speak with our men.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:30.220
Is there anything you need me
to do to help?

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.850
Would you like to give them
an encouraging speech, too?

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.810
N-No thanks, I'll pass!

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:43.440
Here.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:46.200
Thank you.

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.620
I don't think I'll ever
get used to this...

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.260
Exhausted?

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:51.470
I'm all stiff from sitting for so long.

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:54.720
W-We're finally here!

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.980
I'm a little excited to start
exploring Klausner's woods!

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:02.610
Excited to find some new
herbs in the woods?

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:03.690
Yes!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.400
Wait, no!

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.400
Hey!

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.660
We are honored to serve you today, milord.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:17.120
We're honored to have you with us.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:21.630
Our scouting will pale in comparison
to your experience in these woods.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:23.500
Thank you, milord.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.590
And thank you for your
assistance, Lady Saint.

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:27.590
Huh?

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:34.890
Of course. It's my pleasure to assist you.

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:37.020
I'm afraid I'm not accustomed
to these formalities,

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:41.810
so I'd very much appreciate it if you
spoke with me as you did before.

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:44.650
If the Saint wishes it, then I must abide.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:49.240
Thank you, milord. As you wish.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:32.240
What're you looking at?

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.530
Some herbs.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.570
I thought you <i>weren't </i>an alchemist.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.620
Actually, I do work at the capital's
Medicinal Flora Research Institute.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.870
<i>And </i>you're the Saint?

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:44.630
That's right, though I'd say my
Saint work is more of a side job.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:47.540
Is our Kingdom gonna be okay with
that kind of attitude from our Saint?

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.000
--Absolutely!
--Absolutely.

00:16:56.930 --> 00:17:01.480
A-Anyway, it's so lovely here, isn't it?

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:06.770
You think so?
Seems like a normal forest to me.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:12.360
That's what makes it so nice!
You can really become one with nature.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:17.240
You're right about that. Nothin' out here
but nature. That and memories.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:20.120
Spent lots of time in the woods as a kid.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:22.790
You love these woods, don't you?

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:25.670
I-I wouldn't say <i>that</i>.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.170
It's just where I grew up.

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.420
What's your hometown like?

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:38.390
The forests of the capital are nice, too,
though the flora is a bit different.

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:42.220
Huh.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.390
What is it?

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:49.150
Just thinkin' how nice
your hometown must be.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.650
It really is.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:17:59.280
Commander!

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.250
Is something wrong?

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:12.090
We've discovered something that leads us
to believe a dangerous monster is nearby.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.210
What is it?

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:26.560
What <i>is </i>that?!

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.940
Slime digestive juice.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.310
A slime?!

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:33.230
Physical attacks barely
damage them at all,

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:36.150
so we'd like to avoid engaging
it in combat if possible.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:38.490
Does magic work on them, then?

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:42.030
It does. When we do engage them,
we typically do so with magic.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:43.580
Something's still off, though.

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:46.580
All the monsters 'round here
seem to have vanished,

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.790
but somethin' as dangerous as
a slime is still hangin' around?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:51.460
So there <i>are </i>less monsters
present in these woods?

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:56.300
Yeah, I heard you'd killed a bunch,
but I didn't think you'd killed <i>this </i>many.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.300
The same phenomenon
occurred in the capital, too.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.890
Wow. Is that 'cause...

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:04.010
Most likely.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:07.520
Yes, I know.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:10.810
Could you please stop
staring at me like that?

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:17.030
What are your orders, Commander?
Should we proceed?

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:20.160
If there is indeed a miasma
swamp here, then we should.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:27.450
Stay alert, men!
Watch for the traces of dangerous beasts!

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.460
Yes, ser!

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.080
There's one here, too!

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:17.710
<i>Ice Wall</i>!

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:22.840
<i>Fire Lance</i>!

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:30.270
<i>Ice Wall</i>!

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:44.360
Thanks.

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:46.410
No problem, but we can't keep this up...

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.340
Sei!

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.960
Huh? What are you doing here, Aira?!

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:45.090
Um, well, it's a long story...

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:03.150
It's been too long!

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:40.060
Next Time

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:40.060
Return
